        "polymorph",
        "transmutation"
      ],
      "entries": [
        "A cassisian can take the appearance of a dove, a winged humanoid, a dog, or a fish. Normally, this doesn't change its Speed or the attack and damage bonuses for its Strikes, but it might change the damage type Strikes deal (typically to bludgeoning). Any further changes for specific forms are noted below. - Dog size Small; scent (imprecise) 30 feet, Speed 40 feet; Melee jaws +7, Damage 1d6+2 piercing plus Knockdown",
        "- Fish swim Speed 30 feet"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Eye Beams",
      "category": "action",
      "placement": "bot",
      "activity": {
        "unit": "action",
        "number": 2,
        "symbol": "◆◆"
      },
      "traits": [
        "concentrate",
        "divine",
        "evocation"
      ],
      "entries": [
        "The cassisian releases beams of heat or cold from its eyes, dealing 2d6 cold or fire damage (DC 17 basic Reflex save) to all creatures in a 15-foot line. It can't use Eye Beams again for 1d4 rounds."
      ],
